==Battleground==
*20 [[Zoge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*8 [[Znache]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*5 [[Zomboe]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Zigge]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*2 [[Zory|Zories]] spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Kory]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] power up can shoot the Zories, stopping them from [[Burrow|burrowing]]. A hypermaxed [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Flying]] is definitely a valuable asset in this level; additionally, you should try to stack [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] to clear peons and allow Sniper the Cat to hit powerful zombie enemies.

You can also clear this stage by spamming units with decent damage and time between attacks. By stacking these units, you'll deal enough damage to knock back zombies when they are about to burrow, stopping them from burrowing. They'll also deal a lot of damage to Kory, reducing his health. A strong Uber is recommended to take out the Kory quickly in case he plows through your defense and reaches your base.

There is a time limit in this stage, at 3 minutes all zombie enemies (except [[Zoge]]) will stop spawning, giving you a chance to fight Kory without having to worry as much. Stalling and dealing with the zombies before hitting the base is probably the best way to beat the level on 2/3 crowns as well, unless you have the Ubers to deal with everything.

